  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 219 PM MDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nFor Thursday and Friday, the upper ridge remains progged to drift \nnorth and west keeping modest north to northwest flow in place \nacross the Central Rockies. This will tend to slowly diminish \navailable moisture and keep most of afternoon and evening storms\ntied closer to the higher terrain. By Saturday into Sunday, flow \naloft slowly becomes more west to southwest, as broad upper \ntroughing across the West Coast pushes the upper high back south\nand east into the Southern Rockies. This will bring another slow\nuptick in available moisture and storm coverage, especially for the \nhigher terrain along and west of the ContDvd. West to southwest flow \naloft remains progged across the region through the middle of next\nweek, keeping chances of the showers and storms across the region,\nwith the best coverage across the higher terrain.",
